From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfplay: IMFPMediaPlayer volume, balance, mute, effects, FrameStep, SetPosition; DllGetClassObject

- GetVolume/SetVolume (0..1, default 1), GetBalance/SetBalance (-1..1, default 0),
  GetMute/SetMute: round-trip, E_INVALIDARG out of range, E_POINTER, MF_E_SHUTDOWN
  after Shutdown; volume and mute are handed to the session's audio volume
  service when there is one.
- InsertEffect/RemoveEffect/RemoveAllEffects: the effect list (MFT or activator
  only, E_INVALIDARG otherwise; MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST for a duplicate; MF_E_NOT_FOUND
  on removal of an unknown effect); released on Shutdown and with the player.
- SetPosition: 100ns positions as VT_I8/VT_UI8; MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST with no item;
  starts the session at the position while playing, otherwise the next Play
  starts there (GetPosition reports it); posts MFP_EVENT_TYPE_POSITION_SET.
- FrameStep: MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST unless an item is paused; the session cannot step.
- DllGetClassObject is an export now: CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE (no class is
  created through a class factory), E_POINTER for NULL. mfplay.spec changes
  from a stub to a stdcall -private entry.

---
